<title>UK: Texaco restores full capacity at Nerefco refinery.</title>
<headline>Texaco restores full capacity at Nerefco refinery.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Netherlands will return to full capacity on Thursday at the 400,000 barrel per day (bpd) Nerefco refinery it shares with British Petroleum, a trader familiar with the refinery said.  </p>
<p>Texaco, which controls 35 percent of the Pernis and Europoort complex, cut 12.5 percent of its crude runs on March 6 and having initiated a 10 percent cut on March 4.</p>
<p>The 12.5 percent cut was equivalent to a 17,500 bpd reduction in crude runs.</p>
<p>It was not immediately clear whether British Petroleum, which controls 65 percent of the complex, had returned to full capacity.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
</text>
